.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-veil-export-pin 1  "git-veil-export-pin " 
.SH NAME
git\-veil\-export\-pin \- Export this repository\*(Aqs pin\-file for import on another machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-veil export\-pin\fR <\fB\-\-output\fR> [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-store\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIREPO_ID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Export this repository\*(Aqs pin\-file for import on another machine
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Pin\-file destination — must be OUTSIDE the repository worktree
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR [default: origin]
Git remote name
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-store\fR \fI<KEY_STORE>\fR
Key store directory (default: $GIT_VEIL_HOME or $HOME/.git\-veil)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIREPO_ID\fR>
Repository ID (e.g., fara+simbo1905@github.com)
.SH EXTRA
Writes this repository\*(Aqs pin\-file for import on a machine WITHOUT the
signing key (which runs git\-veil trust \-\-import <pin\-file>). Export
requires the same possession proof as trust: an exact match between the
repository\*(Aqs committed owner.verifying and the verifying key derived from
a seed in <key store>/signing\-keys.txt. A machine without the matching
seed cannot export at all — pins originate only from machines holding the
signing key; store\-less machines are consumers, never producers.

\-\-output must point OUTSIDE the repository worktree: a committed pin\-file
would be exactly the self\-supplied anchor the pin model exists to
prevent. Transfer the file out of band (e.g. ssh); its integrity rides
the transport, the same model as known_hosts provisioning.

The printed owner key fingerprint is the human out\-of\-band verification
token: read it to the importing machine\*(Aqs operator and have them compare
it against the repository\*(Aqs committed .git\-veil/trust.json. It is the
single documented derivation with the repository id as the label, so it
is reproducible with stock OS tools; see the fingerprint documentation.

EXAMPLES
  $ git\-veil export\-pin fara+simbo1905@github.com \-\-output /tmp/fara.pin
  $ scp /tmp/fara.pin box:fara.pin               # out of band
  $ git\-veil trust \-\-import fara.pin            # on the target machine
